<title>LEBANON: Most Lebanese T-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>Most Lebanese T-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its December 19 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.80 (13.80)	     14.29 (14.29)</p>
<p>    Six months	    14.95 (15.00)	     16.15 (16.21)</p>
<p>    12 months	     14.55 (14.65)	     17.02 (17.16)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 19.58 (20.04)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
</text>
